  "text": "Adopted Codes and Regulations for the Building Department | Mesa County\nSkip to main content\nStage 1 Fire Restrictions enacted\nEffective beginning 12:01 a.m. Friday, Sept. 4, 2026, until further notice. These restrictions apply to all private land and BLM managed public lands within the boundaries of the Grand Junction Field Office. For more information visit the Fire Restrictions webpage.\nTranslate\nMain navigation\nMENU\nMENU\nResident Resources\nBusiness Resources\nDepartments and Services\nContact Us\nJobs\nADA\nEvents\nNews\nTranslate\nBreadcrumb\nHome\nDepartments and Services\nCommunity Development\nBuilding Department\nAdopted Codes and Regulations For The Building Department\nAdopted Codes and Regulations for the Building Department\nAdopted codes\nThe 2026 NEC and 2024 Colorado Plumbing and Fuel Gas Code will be effective January 1,2027.\nIn compliance with HB21-1110 Mesa County Ordinance adopting and amending Building Codes  are unable to be posted on this site.\nFor assistance contact us at 970-244-1631\n2021 International Energy Conservation Code\n2024 International Building Code\n2024 International Existing Building Code\n2024 International Mechanical Code\n2024 International Residential Code\nState Adopted Codes\nColorado Model and Solar Ready Code\nColorado Plumbing and Fuel Gas Code\n2021 International Fuel Gas Code\n2021 International Plumbing Code\n2023 National Electric Code (no link available)\nLocal requirements\nSnow and wind loads by area\nArea\nGround snow load\nnon-reducible\nWind stagnation\npressure at 30 ft. ht.\nBasic wind speed\n(residential only)\nGrand Junction\nand surrounding area\n30#\n13\n104\nDeBeque\n30#\n13\n104\nMesa\n40#\n13\n104\nPowderhorn\n90#\n17\n104\nMolina\n40#\n13\n104\nPlateau City\n40#\n13\n104\nCollbran\n40#\n13\n104\nVega Area\n70#\n13\n104\nMesa Lakes\n100#\n13\n104\nLittle Park\n30#\n13\n104\nGlade Park Store\n& within a 2 mile radius\n30#\n13\n104\nGlade Park Area\n(other)\nContact the\nBuilding